{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Heavy Rainfall Day (HRD) Definition \u2014 R99th Threshold\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements the HRD definition described in the manuscript:\n",
    "\n",
    "> After completing the quality control of the rainfall dataset, we defined a heavy rainfall day for the state of\n",
    "> NSW. For the threshold of a heavy rainfall day (hereafter referred to as HRD), we used the 99th percentile\n",
    "> (R99th) index, as defined by the Expert Team on Climate Change Detection and Indices (ETCCDI) (Alexander\n",
    "> & Herold, 2019). We considered only wet days (rainfall \u2265 1.00 mm) in the threshold calculation. This was\n",
    "> necessary due to the rainfall gradient east-west of NSW, where average annual rainfall decreases inland,\n",
    "> resulting in a highly skewed distribution with many zero-rainfall days. Including zero-rainfall values in the\n",
    "> percentile calculation would have significantly lowered the heavy rainfall threshold for stations in the far west\n",
    "> of NSW. To provide a consistent record, we used AGCD and calculated the 99th percentile of daily rainfall\n",
    "> amounts across all wet days from 1900\u20132024 at each 5 km grid cell across NSW. We then extracted the 99th\n",
    "> percentile value for each grid cell at the nearest gauge location. Once we determined the 99th percentile\n",
    "> threshold values for all 5,429 stations, we defined an HRD for NSW as any day on which at least one station\n",
    "> in the network recorded rainfall exceeding its 99th percentile threshold.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pipeline (4 steps)**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Compute the AGCD 99th percentile grid (wet days only, 1900\u20132024, 5 km resolution) \n",
    "2. Extract the R99th threshold at each of the 5,429 station locations (nearest grid cell) \n",
    "3. Flag each station's own exceedance days (bridge step, required before Step 4) \n",
    "4. Define the network-wide HRD = any day with \u22651 station exceeding its threshold \n",
    "\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 0 \u2014 Config"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import xarray as xr\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Paths (edit these) ---------------------------------------------------\n",
    "AGCD_FILE_PATTERN      = \"/g/data/zv2/agcd/v1-0-3/precip/total/r005/01day/agcd_v1_precip_total_r005_daily_*.nc\"\n",
    "LANDSEA_MASK_FILE       = \"/path/to/mask_landsea.nc\"\n",
    "NSW_MASK_FILE           = \"/path/to/precip_calib_0.25_maskforCAus.nc\"\n",
    "PERCENTILE_GRID_FILE    = \"/path/to/precip_percentiles_1900_2024.nc\"\n",
    "\n",
    "STATION_LIST_FILE       = \"/path/to/5429_Station_list.xlsx\"          # must contain Station Number, Lat, Lon\n",
    "CLEAN_STATION_DIR       = Path(\"/path/to/parquet_network_QC\")         # output of Data_Filtration_clean.ipynb\n",
    "EXTREME_DAYS_DIR        = Path(\"/path/to/Extreme_Rainfall_Days\")\n",
    "HRD_OUTPUT_FILE         = \"/path/to/HRD_dates.xlsx\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Parameters (must match the manuscript methods paragraph) ------------\n",
    "WET_DAY_THRESHOLD_MM = 1.00      # only wet days count toward the percentile\n",
    "PERCENTILES          = [0.90, 0.99]   # R99th defines the HRD threshold; 90th kept for reference"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 \u2014 Compute the AGCD 99th percentile grid\n",
    "\n",
    "> We used AGCD and calculated the 99th percentile of daily rainfall amounts across all wet days from\n",
    "> 1900\u20132024 at each 5 km grid cell across NSW.\n",
    "\n",
    "Adapted from `20CRv3_5.ipynb`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from dask.distributed import Client\n",
    "\n",
    "client = Client(n_workers=8, threads_per_worker=7, memory_limit=\"9GB\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def _preprocess(ds):\n",
    "    # Spatial subset covering Australia\n",
    "    return ds.precip.sel(lat=slice(-45, -5), lon=slice(105, 160))\n",
    "\n",
    "precip = xr.open_mfdataset(AGCD_FILE_PATTERN, parallel=False, preprocess=_preprocess)\n",
    "precip = precip.chunk({\"time\": -1, \"lat\": 25, \"lon\": 25}).persist()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Land-sea + Central-Australia masks, interpolated onto the AGCD grid\n",
    "landsea_mask = xr.open_dataset(LANDSEA_MASK_FILE)\n",
    "nsw_mask     = xr.open_dataset(NSW_MASK_FILE)\n",
    "\n",
    "if \"time\" in landsea_mask.dims:\n",
    "    landsea_mask = landsea_mask.sel(time=\"1984-06-06T11:00:00\")\n",
    "\n",
    "landsea_mask = landsea_mask.interp(latitude=precip.lat, longitude=precip.lon, method=\"nearest\")\n",
    "nsw_mask     = nsw_mask.interp(latitude=precip.lat, longitude=precip.lon, method=\"nearest\")\n",
    "\n",
    "precip_masked = precip.where((landsea_mask[\"lsm\"] > 0.5) & (nsw_mask[\"mask\"] == 1))\n",
    "precip_masked = precip_masked.drop_vars([\"latitude\", \"longitude\"], errors=\"ignore\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only grid cells with a complete time series\n",
    "valid_cells = precip_masked[\"precip\"].notnull().mean(dim=\"time\")\n",
    "precip_masked = precip_masked.where(valid_cells)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Only wet days (>= 1 mm) count toward the percentile -- otherwise the many\n",
    "# zero-rainfall days in western NSW would drag the threshold down.\n",
    "precip_wet = precip_masked[\"precip\"].where(precip_masked[\"precip\"] >= WET_DAY_THRESHOLD_MM)\n",
    "\n",
    "quantiles = precip_wet.quantile(PERCENTILES, dim=\"time\")\n",
    "precip_90th = quantiles.sel(quantile=0.90).drop_vars(\"quantile\")\n",
    "precip_99th = quantiles.sel(quantile=0.99).drop_vars(\"quantile\")\n",
    "\n",
    "percentile_ds = xr.Dataset({\"precip_90th\": precip_90th, \"precip_99th\": precip_99th})\n",
    "percentile_ds.to_netcdf(PERCENTILE_GRID_FILE, mode=\"w\", compute=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Saved 90th/99th percentile grid to {PERCENTILE_GRID_FILE}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 \u2014 Extract the R99th threshold at each station\n",
    "\n",
    "> We then extracted the 99th percentile value for each grid cell at the nearest gauge location. Once we\n",
    "> determined the 99th percentile threshold values for all 5,429 stations...\n",
    "\n",
    "Adapted from `Data Filtration.ipynb`. Nearest-neighbour lookup from the percentile grid onto each station's\n",
    "Lat/Lon."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "percentile_ds  = xr.open_dataset(PERCENTILE_GRID_FILE)\n",
    "precip_99th_da = percentile_ds[\"precip_99th\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "stations_df = pd.read_excel(STATION_LIST_FILE, sheet_name=\"Sheet1\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def nearest_r99(row):\n",
    "    value = precip_99th_da.sel(lat=row[\"Lat\"], lon=row[\"Lon\"], method=\"nearest\").values\n",
    "    return round(float(np.ravel(value)[0]), 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "stations_df[\"R1_99\"] = stations_df.apply(nearest_r99, axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "with pd.ExcelWriter(STATION_LIST_FILE, engine=\"openpyxl\", mode=\"a\", if_sheet_exists=\"overlay\") as writer:\n",
    "    stations_df.to_excel(writer, index=False, sheet_name=\"Sheet1\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"R99th threshold assigned to {stations_df['R1_99'].notna().sum()} of {len(stations_df)} stations\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 \u2014 Flag each station's own exceedance days\n",
    "\n",
    "Bridge step required before Step 4: for every station, keep only the days where its rainfall exceeded its own\n",
    "R99th threshold. Adapted from `Data Filtration.ipynb`, but reads from the **quality-controlled** station data\n",
    "(`parquet_network_QC`, produced by `Data_Filtration_clean.ipynb`) rather than the raw data the original\n",
    "notebook used \u2014 since the manuscript defines HRDs *after* QC."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "EXTREME_DAYS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "r99_lookup = stations_df.set_index(\"Station Number\")[\"R1_99\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "for file_path in sorted(CLEAN_STATION_DIR.glob(\"*.parquet\")):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        station_number = int(file_path.stem)\n",
    "    except ValueError:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    if station_number not in r99_lookup.index:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    threshold = r99_lookup.loc[station_number]\n",
    "    df = pd.read_parquet(file_path)\n",
    "    df[\"Rainfall\"] = pd.to_numeric(df[\"Rainfall\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    exceedance_days = df[df[\"Rainfall\"] > threshold]\n",
    "    if not exceedance_days.empty:\n",
    "        exceedance_days.to_parquet(EXTREME_DAYS_DIR / file_path.name, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Saved per-station exceedance-day files to {EXTREME_DAYS_DIR}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 \u2014 Define the network-wide Heavy Rainfall Day (HRD)\n",
    "\n",
    "> we defined an HRD for NSW as any day on which at least one station in the network recorded rainfall\n",
    "> exceeding its 99th percentile threshold.\n",
    "\n",
    "Adapted from `Important Codes.ipynb`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "station_count_by_date = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for file_path in sorted(EXTREME_DAYS_DIR.glob(\"*.parquet\")):\n",
    "    df = pd.read_parquet(file_path)[[\"Year\", \"Month\", \"Day\", \"Rainfall\"]]\n",
    "    df = df[df[\"Rainfall\"] > 0]   # rows here already exceed threshold; this just guards against NaNs\n",
    "    for _, row in df.iterrows():\n",
    "        date_str = datetime(int(row[\"Year\"]), int(row[\"Month\"]), int(row[\"Day\"])).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n",
    "        station_count_by_date[date_str] = station_count_by_date.get(date_str, 0) + 1\n",
    "\n",
    "date_range = pd.date_range(start=\"1858-01-01\", end=\"2024-12-31\")\n",
    "daily_df = pd.DataFrame({\"Date\": date_range})\n",
    "daily_df[\"Station Count\"] = (\n",
    "    daily_df[\"Date\"].dt.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\").map(station_count_by_date).fillna(0).astype(int)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# HRD = at least one station exceeded its threshold that day\n",
    "hrd_dates = daily_df[daily_df[\"Station Count\"] > 0].copy()\n",
    "hrd_dates[\"Date\"] = hrd_dates[\"Date\"].dt.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n",
    "\n",
    "hrd_dates.to_excel(HRD_OUTPUT_FILE, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"Total HRDs identified (1858-2024): {len(hrd_dates):,}\")\n",
    "hrd_dates.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5 \u2014 Sanity check"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_days = (pd.Timestamp(\"2024-12-31\") - pd.Timestamp(\"1858-01-01\")).days + 1\n",
    "print(f\"Total calendar days 1858-2024: {total_days:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total HRDs:                    {len(hrd_dates):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"HRDs as % of all days:         {len(hrd_dates) / total_days * 100:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
